# {{ component.name }}

This directory is the research pipeline for {{ blueprint.project.name }}. Its
checked-in fixture is generated from a fixed seed and contains no human,
patient, employer, or third-party data. The baseline model exists to test the
pipeline contract. It does not support medical or clinical use.

## First setup

Run commands through mise. The template does not write `uv.lock` because the
repository layout contract requires uv to create its own lockfile.

```bash
mise //{{ component.path }}:lock
mise //{{ component.path }}:ci
```

Commit `uv.lock` and `dvc.lock` after reviewing the resolved packages and DVC
stage hashes. `mise //{{ component.path }}:install` and every CI task use the
lockfile with `--locked`.

## Pipeline

`dvc.yaml` defines three local stages. `build_fixture` writes a deterministic
JSONL dataset, `train` fits a small threshold baseline, and `evaluate` writes
metrics plus content-hash provenance. None of the stages make a network call.

```bash
mise //{{ component.path }}:dvc:dag
mise //{{ component.path }}:repro
mise //{{ component.path }}:verify
```

The fixture tests repository wiring only. Replace the baseline when a research
question needs another model, but keep model inputs, parameters, code, outputs,
and compact metrics declared in DVC.

## Data and evaluation extensions

`registries/datasets.json` is the dataset identity boundary. Add public or
privately governed datasets there only after adding a matching rights record.
Keep source-specific download and validation code in this component, then add
its checked manifest to the relevant DVC stage. Do not put credentials or
private artifact bytes in Git.

`registries/downstream-evaluations.json` records consumers outside this
component. A consumer pins the producer project, artifact path, schema version,
and content hash. Cross-project code imports are not allowed; exchange a
versioned artifact or use an API.

The committed manifests have separate jobs:

- `manifests/rights.json` records the authority to use each source.
- `manifests/decision-provenance.json` points to the platform decisions behind
  the generated structure.
- `outputs/provenance.json` binds one reproduced result to exact input hashes.

The CLI emits one JSON event per stage on standard output. The resource keys
match the repository OpenTelemetry identity contract. A deployed project may
replace the local emitter with an OpenTelemetry SDK and exporter after it has
defined redaction, queue bounds, retention, and an operator.

## CI integration

The stable CI entry point is:

```bash
mise //{{ component.path }}:ci
```

It runs formatting, Ruff, ty, pytest with 90 percent line coverage, the DVC
graph, provenance verification, and the package build. CI can publish
`coverage.xml`, `metrics/metrics.json`, and `outputs/provenance.json`. A shared
workflow should call the mise task instead of repeating these commands.
